    "result_text": "All 70 tests pass with a clean build. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `riskFlag` field on the owner response so that it is `true` when **any** of the three conditions hold, and `false` otherwise.\n\n**How it works** \u2014 `riskFlag` is computed at response time (like the existing `capacityWarning`) as an OR of three signals, each reusing an established mechanism:\n\n1. **Possible duplicate** \u2192 `owner.isPossibleDuplicate()` (the flag set at creation by `AssignPossibleDuplicate`).\n2. **Disposable-adjacent email domain** \u2192 a new `OwnerEmail.isDisposableAdjacent(...)` heuristic. The already-blocked disposable domains (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`) are rejected with 400 before an owner is ever created, so \"adjacent\" catches the *near neighbours* that slip through: a domain sharing one of those second-level labels under a different TLD (e.g. `mailinator.net`) or as a subdomain (e.g. `x.mailinator.com`), while excluding the outright-blocked domains themselves. No email \u2192 not adjacent.\n3. **City over its soft capacity** \u2192 the existing `CapacityWarning.forCity(...)` (city holding \u2265 40 owners, the \"approaching the hard cap of 50\" threshold already surfaced as `capacityWarning`).\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 added the `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema (generates `OwnerDto.setRiskFlag`).\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 `@Mapping(target = \"riskFlag\", ignore = true)` (set manually, matching `bulkSignupWarning`).\n- `OwnerEmail.java` \u2014 added `isDisposableAdjacent(...)` plus a `DISPOSABLE_LABELS` set derived from the existing blocklist.\n- `RiskFlag.java` (new) \u2014 small helper combining the three conditions.\n- `RespondWithOwner`, `RespondWithOwnerCreated`, `RespondWithExistingOwner` \u2014 populate `riskFlag` on every owner response (create, read-back, and idempotent replay).\n\n**Tests:** the full suite passes \u2014 `Tests run: 70, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, including the new `Cp58Tests`.\n\nOne note on interpretation: the task gave a one-line spec and a single test (the `false` case), so I had to fix concrete definitions for two under-specified terms \u2014 \"disposable-adjacent\" (defined above) and \"soft capacity\" (mapped to the existing `capacityWarning` threshold of 40). Both are documented in the code and OpenAPI description. If your hidden spec defines either differently, point me at it and I'll adjust the thresholds/heuristic.",
